 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Purpose with the same subject: um … zu versus damit",
     "texto": [
      "1. **um … zu + Infinitiv**: Used when the subject of the main action and that of the final clause is exactly the same person or entity: **Ich lerne Deutsch, um in Berlin zu studieren** (I study German to study in Berlin). The particle **um** is placed at the start of the final group (after the comma) and **zu + Infinitiv** goes at the very end.",
      "2. **damit**: If the subjects of both clauses are different, **damit** with a full subordinate clause must be used: **Ich erkläre es langsam, damit du mich verstehst** (I explain it slowly so that you understand me).",
      "3. **Separable at the end**: If the final infinitive is separable, **zu** is inserted: **um mich vorzubereiten** (to prepare myself); **um mich auszuruhen** (to rest)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Connector",
     "columnas": [
